cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this audit framework, please cite the manuscript; if you use the code directly, cite this archived release."
title: "Batch-confound audit for public transcriptomic datasets"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a four-stage design-admissibility audit for public
  transcriptomic datasets, with the derived results and figures for a
  methodological audit of 14 contrast-units across 12 GEO series in
  perioperative neurocognitive disorder and traumatic brain injury. The audit
  applies four defences in order (label verifiability; a three-gate batch test combining
  structural entanglement, technical separability and nesting; global-shift
  diagnosis; external gene-set validation) and returns one of four verdicts --
  stop, correct, proceed or normalize -- per contrast-unit.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-22"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22899702"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eagle-wk/pocd-batch-audit"
url: "https://github.com/eagle-wk/pocd-batch-audit"
keywords:
  - batch effect
  - confounding
  - GEO
  - reproducibility
  - transcriptomics
  - methodological audit
  - perioperative neurocognitive disorder
  - traumatic brain injury
